        "title": "BepiColombo’s Mercury arrival begins (Official ESA broadcast)",
        "description": "Join us live on 3 September as ESA/JAXA's BepiColombo mission takes the first critical step towards arriving at Mercury. \n\nAfter travelling through the inner Solar System together for eight years, BepiColombo's Mercury Transfer Module (MTM) will separate from the rest of the stacked spacecraft on 3 September 2026. This marks the beginning of one of the most complex planetary arrival sequences ever attempted by ESA. \n\nBroadcast live from ESA's European Space Operations Centre (ESOC) in Darmstadt, Germany, the programme includes live views from the iconic Main Control Room, expert analysis, behind-the-scenes insights, and the first expected signal from the spacecraft following separation. \n\nThis is a moment eight years in the making that you don’t want to miss!\n\nLivestream schedule (CES...",
